            "description": "CRIT threshold for how far the checkpoint has run through the redo log, in percent of `Innodb_checkpoint_max_age`. From 100 InnoDB puts a synchronous wait into every write operation, and a redo log that is too small sits pinned there under load. Only evaluated on a server that publishes its checkpoint age. Supports Nagios ranges.",
